> What do you mean by "clear the way" to the VS?

I mean clearing all the levels down to there -- exploring them
and killing all the monsters on them.  Yes, I know speed runners
probably don't bother with this, but that omission would very
much complicate the ascension run for them.

> Gehennom is short if you don't explore it completely.

Gehennom is not short.  Gehennom is at least twenty levels long,
and furthermore each of those twenty levels takes several times
as long to explore as a typical pre-Castle level.

If you're *skipping* most of it every single time, in order to
avoid being bored to tears, and arguing that this is what everyone
should do, then you're making my point for me.  You wouldn't be
skipping as much of it as you can possibly manage to skip if it
weren't boring.

A really successful revision of Gehennom, IMO, would be one that
results in people no longer *wanting* to skip large parts of it.

