The demon-prince lairs actively prevent this by having gratuitous
undiggable walls blocking the places you'd most like to dig.  (You
can dig holes in the floor, but that only helps on downward trips.
Half of every trip is going the other way, where holes are useless.)
The maze levels allow digging, but you have to do it the slow way,
1 tile at a time, because even though you have typically accumulated
about eighty wands of digging they don't make the process any faster
(in terms of _player_ time; I realize they do use fewer game turns,
but the player does not usually perceive time that way) than a pick.

